data collection or in data dissemination. (e.g., a time series could be available at annual frequency but the underlying data are compiled monthly). Therefore, \"Frequency\" can be broken down into \"Frequency - data collection\" and \"Frequency - data dissemination\".","texts":{"en":"If a data series has a constant time interval between its observations, this interval determines the frequency of the series (e.g. monthly, quarterly, yearly). \"Frequency\" - also called \"periodicity\" - may refer to several stages in the production process, e.g. in data collection or in data dissemination. (e.g., a time series could be available at annual frequency but the underlying data are compiled monthly). Therefore, \"Frequency\" can be broken down into \"Frequency - data collection\" and \"Frequency - data dissemination\"."}},{"type":"TYPE","text":"Cross-domain concept","texts":{"en":"Cross-domain concept"}},{"type":"RECOMMENDED_REPRESENTATION","text":"Code list","texts":{"en":"Code list"}},{"type":"RELATED_TERMS","text":"Frequency of data collection; Frequency of dissemination","texts":{"en":"Frequency of data collection; Frequency of dissemination"}},{"type":"OTHER_LINKS","text":"Code list CL_FREQ (https://sdmx.org/?page_id=3215)","texts":{"en":"Code list CL_FREQ (https://sdmx.org/?page_id=3215)"}},{"type":"CODELIST_ID","text":"CL_FREQ","texts":{"en":"CL_FREQ"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"2","texts":{"en":"2"}},{"type":"CONTEXT","text":"The concept refers to the country, geographical or political group of countries or regions within a country. The concept is subject to a variety of hierarchies, as countries comprise territorial entities that are states (as understood by international law and practice), regions and other territorial entities that are not states but for which statistical data are produced internationally on a separate and independent basis.","texts":{"en":"The concept refers to the country, geographical or political group of countries or regions within a country. The concept is subject to a variety of hierarchies, as countries comprise territorial entities that are states (as understood by international law and practice), regions and other territorial entities that are not states but for which statistical data are produced internationally on a separate and independent basis."}},{"type":"RELATED_TERMS","text":"Counterpart reference area","texts":{"en":"Counterpart reference area"}},{"type":"OTHER_LINKS","text":"Code list CL_AREA (https://sdmx.org/?page_id=3215, See under \"Geographical area\")","texts":{"en":"Code list CL_AREA (https://sdmx.org/?page_id=3215, See under \"Geographical area\")"}},{"type":"CODELIST_ID","text":"CL_AREA","texts":{"en":"CL_AREA"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"17","texts":{"en":"17"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"5","texts":{"en":"5"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"6","texts":{"en":"6"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"8","texts":{"en":"8"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"2","texts":{"en":"2"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"3","texts":{"en":"3"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"4","texts":{"en":"4"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"1","texts":{"en":"1"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"9","texts":{"en":"9"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"10","texts":{"en":"10"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"12","texts":{"en":"12"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"13","texts":{"en":"13"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"16","texts":{"en":"16"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"17","texts":{"en":"17"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"18","texts":{"en":"18"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"19","texts":{"en":"19"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"21","texts":{"en":"21"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"22","texts":{"en":"22"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"23","texts":{"en":"23"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"24","texts":{"en":"24"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"26","texts":{"en":"26"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"27","texts":{"en":"27"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"28","texts":{"en":"28"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"29","texts":{"en":"29"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"30","texts":{"en":"30"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"31","texts":{"en":"31"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"33","texts":{"en":"33"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"34","texts":{"en":"34"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"35","texts":{"en":"35"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"36","texts":{"en":"36"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"37","texts":{"en":"37"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"38","texts":{"en":"38"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"39","texts":{"en":"39"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"40","texts":{"en":"40"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"41","texts":{"en":"41"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"42","texts":{"en":"42"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER"},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"540","texts":{"en":"540"}},{"type":"CONTEXT","text":"The unit of measure is a quantity or increment by which something is counted or described, such as kg, mm, C, F, monetary units such as Euro or US dollar, simple number counts or index numbers. The unit of measure has a type (e.g. currency) and, in connection with the unit multiplier, provides the level of detail for the value of the variable. For data messages, the concept is usually represented by codes. For metadata messages the concept is usually represented by free text.","texts":{"en":"The unit of measure is a quantity or increment by which something is counted or described, such as kg, mm, C, F, monetary units such as Euro or US dollar, simple number counts or index numbers. The unit of measure has a type (e.g. currency) and, in connection with the unit multiplier, provides the level of detail for the value of the variable. For data messages, the concept is usually represented by codes. For metadata messages the concept is usually represented by free text."}},{"type":"CODELIST_ID","text":"CL_UNIT_MEASURE","texts":{"en":"CL_UNIT_MEASURE"}},{"type":"CONTEXT","text":"Adjustments may be associated with changes in definitions, exchange rates, prices, seasons and other factors. Adjustments are in particular applied to compile consistent time series, but the concept is also used for describing adjustments related to other types of data. Adjustment can be distinguished from editing and imputation, in that before adjustment, the data are already of sufficient quality to be considered usable.","texts":{"en":"Adjustments may be associated with changes in definitions, exchange rates, prices, seasons and other factors. Adjustments are in particular applied to compile consistent time series, but the concept is also used for describing adjustments related to other types of data. Adjustment can be distinguished from editing and imputation, in that before adjustment, the data are already of sufficient quality to be considered usable."}},{"type":"RECOMMENDED_REPRESENTATION","text":"String","texts":{"en":"String"}},{"type":"RELATED_TERMS","text":"Price adjustment; Seasonal adjustment","texts":{"en":"Price adjustment; Seasonal adjustment"}},{"id":"ORDER","title":"ORDER","type":"ORDER","text":"92","texts":{"en":"92"}},{"type":"CONTEXT","text":"In some databases, it is referred to as SCALE, MAGNITUDE or POWER, e.g. UNIT_MULT 6 means that observations are in millions.","texts":{"en":"In some databases, it is referred to as SCALE, MAGNITUDE or POWER, e.g. UNIT_MULT 6 means that observations are in millions."}},{"type":"OTHER_LINKS","text":"Code list CL_UNIT_MULT (https://sdmx.org/?page_id=3215)","texts":{"en":"Code list CL_UNIT_MULT (https://sdmx.org/?page_id=3215)"}},{"type":"CODELIST_ID","text":"CL_UNIT_MULT","texts":{"en":"CL_UNIT_MULT"}},{"type":"CONTEXT","text":"Examples of such time transformations are growth rates, cumulative sums over N periods and moving averages. Operations on time series not entailing a \"time\" component (e.g. ratios) are not to be considered as time transformations.","texts":{"en":"Examples of such time transformations are growth rates, cumulative sums over N periods and moving averages. Operations on time series not entailing a \"time\" component (e.g. ratios) are not to be considered as time transformations."}},{"type":"CODELIST_ID","text":"CL_TRANSFORMATION","texts":{"en":"CL_TRANSFORMATION"}},{"type":"CONTEXT","text":"A decimal is a fraction that has a denominator of a power of ten, the power depending on or deciding the decimal place. It is indicated by a decimal point to the left of the numerator, the denominator being omitted. Zeros are inserted between the point and the numerator, if necessary, to obtain the correct decimal place. Examples of decimals are 0.04 = 4/100 or 0.126 = 126/1000.","texts":{"en":"A decimal is a fraction that has a denominator of a power of ten, the power depending on or deciding the decimal place. It is indicated by a decimal point to the left of the numerator, the denominator being omitted. Zeros are inserted between the point and the numerator, if necessary, to obtain the correct decimal place. Examples of decimals are 0.04 = 4/100 or 0.126 = 126/1000."}},{"type":"OTHER_LINKS","text":"Code list CL_DECIMALS (https://sdmx.org/?page_id=3215)","texts":{"en":"Code list CL_DECIMALS (https://sdmx.org/?page_id=3215)"}},{"type":"CODELIST_ID","text":"CL_DECIMALS","texts":{"en":"CL_DECIMALS"}},{"type":"CONTEXT","text":"This item is normally coded and uses codes providing information about the status of a value, with respect to events such as \"break\", \"estimated value\", \"forecast\", \"missing value\", or \"provisional value\". In some cases, there is more than one event that may have influenced the value (e.g. a break in methodology may be accompanied with the fact that an observation is an estimate).","texts":{"en":"This item is normally coded and uses codes providing information about the status of a value, with respect to events such as \"break\", \"estimated value\", \"forecast\", \"missing value\", or \"provisional value\". In some cases, there is more than one event that may have influenced the value (e.g. a break in methodology may be accompanied with the fact that an observation is an estimate)."}},{"type":"OTHER_LINKS","text":"Code list CL_OBS_STATUS (https://sdmx.org/?page_id=3215); Possible Ways of Implementing CL_OBS_STATUS Code List (https://sdmx.org/wp-content/uploads/CL_OBS_STATUS_implementation_20-10-2014.doc)","texts":{"en":"Code list CL_OBS_STATUS (https://sdmx.org/?page_id=3215); Possible Ways of Implementing CL_OBS_STATUS Code List (https://sdmx.org/wp-content/uploads/CL_OBS_STATUS_implementation_20-10-2014.doc)"}},{"type":"CODELIST_ID","text":"CL_OBS_STATUS","texts":{"en":"CL_OBS_STATUS"}},{"type":"CONTEXT","text":"This concept is related to data and determines the exact status of the value. i.e. if a specific value is confidential or not. This concept is always coded, i.e. it takes its value from the respective code list.","texts":{"en":"This concept is related to data and determines the exact status of the value. i.e. if a specific value is confidential or not. This concept is always coded, i.e. it takes its value from the respective code list."}},{"type":"RELATED_TERMS","text":"Confidentiality; Confidentiality - data treatment; Confidentiality - policy; Confidentiality - redistribution authorisation policy","texts":{"en":"Confidentiality; Confidentiality - data treatment; Confidentiality - policy; Confidentiality - redistribution authorisation policy"}},{"type":"OTHER_LINKS","text":"Code list CL_CONF_STATUS (https://sdmx.org/?page_id=3215)","texts":{"en":"Code list CL_CONF_STATUS (https://sdmx.org/?page_id=3215)"}},{"type":"CODELIST_ID","text":"CL_CONF_STATUS","texts":{"en":"CL_CONF_STATUS"}},{"type":"CONTEXT","text":"The technical time format and its related code list are part of the technical standards for SDMX-EDI and SDMX-XML.","texts":{"en":"The technical time format and its related code list are part of the technical standards for SDMX-EDI and SDMX-XML."}},{"type":"OTHER_LINKS","text":"Code list CL_TIME_FORMAT (https://sdmx.org/?page_id=3215)","texts":{"en":"Code list CL_TIME_FORMAT (https://sdmx.org/?page_id=3215)"}},{"type":"CODELIST_ID","text":"CL_TIME_FORMAT","texts":{"en":"CL_TIME_FORMAT"}}]}},"errors":[]}